# party — turn-reset on room entry, scripted sequence per location

"The Party" by Bernd Eickhoff version social_hell

on go Room:destination:
    turn = 0
    parent

Room kitchen "A cramped kitchen, busy with party overflow."
    east: living room

    on turn 0:
        say "You wander into the kitchen."

    on turn 1:
        say "A blonde and John are in the corner. They have only eyes for each other."

    on turn 2:
        say "You feel your presence is an inconvenience."
        go living room

Room living room "The main room. Music thumps."
    west: kitchen
    north: garden

    on turn 0:
        say "You drift into the living room."

    on turn 1:
        say "A group huddles around the TV. Nobody looks up."

    on turn 2:
        say "The silence is deafening."
        go garden

Room garden "A small patio. Cold air and the smell of cigarettes."
    south: living room

    on turn 0:
        say "You slip out into the back garden."

    on turn 1:
        say "Two people are deep in conversation. One angles away as you approach."

    on turn 2:
        say "Even outside you can't escape the awkwardness."
        go kitchen

test
    test "kitchen sequence".
    test "cycling".

test "kitchen sequence"
    . "wander into the kitchen"
    wait. "only eyes for each other"
    wait. "inconvenience"

test "cycling"
    wait. "drift into the living room"
    wait. "Nobody looks up"
    wait. "garden"
